 glass when rival dragons fought above massed armies. The crowns abandoned the survivors, who learned to organize water, defense, trade, and burial without inherited rank."],"layout":["recognizable regional threshold","primary public route","restricted or dangerous edge"],"crowdRhythm":{"morning":"Workers, soldiers, and markets establish the district’s practical rhythm.","afternoon":"Trade, authority, and travel overlap.","evening":"Taverns, courts, houses, and private meetings reshape public life.","late_night":"Curfews, nightlife, watches, and clandestine movement dominate.","overnight":"Only essential, military, covert, or explicitly continuous locations remain active."},"conversationHooks":["The Cinder Saint may be the missing heir.","A nameless vault can erase legal caste.","One new dragon egg will hatch only before people who surrender ownership."],"stableFacts":["The glassed center of the realm, populated by refugees, deserters, scavengers, healers, free camps, outlaw markets, and people building law without nobles.","Aster Field became black glass when rival dragons fought above massed armies. The crowns abandoned the survivors, who learned to organize water, defense, trade, and burial without inherited rank.","Primary ruling power: Contested; Broken Chain influence."],"localEtiquette":["Caste rules vary by controlling faction.","Private access is never implied by familiarity alone."],"publicHistory":["Aster Field became black glass when rival dragons fought above massed armies. The crowns abandoned the survivors, who learned to organize water, defense, trade, and burial without inherited rank."],"recurringPeople":[{"label":"district regulars","role":"workers, residents, retainers, travelers, and watchers","rhythm":"They recognize repeated routines and react to banner changes."}],"activityNotes":{"travel":"Weather and war may alter routes.","observation":"Observed facts must come from authored lore or active events."},"accessNotes":["Military, noble, sacred, and private thresholds require explicit access."],"weatherNotes":["Glass storms can strip exposed skin and reveal buried ruins.","Cold ash nights make every lit shelter a promise and a risk."],"storySeeds":["The Cinder Saint may be the missing heir.","A nameless vault can erase legal caste.","One new dragon egg will hatch only before people who surrender ownership."]},"metadata":{"rulingPower":"Contested; Broken Chain influence","tags":["scarred","improvised","dangerously hopeful","haunted by war"],"source":"vharadren_content_pack_v1"}},{"slug":"dragonbone-citadel","name":"Dragonbone Citadel","districtSlug":"crownspire","category":"castle","locationType":"venue","hours":{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"},"description":"The Vaelorian royal fortress rises through the ribs of the covenant dragon Azhuriel, combining palace, war room, archive, barracks, and ceremonial prison.","backstory":"The first emperors built chambers between the fossilized ribs rather than moving them, claiming the bones consented. Hairline fractures now glow whenever the throne issues an unlawful decree.","socialTexture":"Nobles move through sunlit galleries while servants, petitioners, hostages, and guards navigate older passages inside the bones. Court life is intimate because privacy itself is a rationed privilege.","activities":["royal audiences","court intrigue","archive research","formal feasts","guard duty"],"visualAnchors":["colossal ivory ribs","black-and-gold towers","oath banners","ash-lit courtyards"],"secret":"The deepest rib chamber preserves Azhuriel’s final memory of the uncrowned covenant.","storySeeds":["A servant door opens onto a sealed royal nursery.","A feast guest carries the same poison used in 701 AF."],"accessNotes":["Public galleries require sponsorship or an audience writ.","Royal apartments, bone crypts, and war rooms require explicit story access."],"id":"2d000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007","worldId":"10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013","parentLocationId":"2d000000