ork, faction overlap, or repeated nights under lantern law.","privateTension":"Their loyalties and private wants do not align perfectly.","knowledgeScope":"direct","authored":true},{"sourceSlug":"rorik-pell","targetSlug":"captain-seraphine-vale","relationshipType":"trusted contact","affinity":0.7,"trust":0.64,"tension":0.12,"publicDynamic":"They know one another through shattered-coast, house work, faction overlap, or repeated nights under lantern law.","privateTension":"Their loyalties and private wants do not align perfectly.","knowledgeScope":"direct","authored":true},{"sourceSlug":"delphine-lantern","targetSlug":"rorik-pell","relationshipType":"house colleague","affinity":0.8,"trust":0.74,"tension":0.1,"publicDynamic":"Delphine Lantern keeps Rorik Pell on the house books and in the Compact’s protection.","privateTension":"The house is both shelter and the thing that keeps them performing.","knowledgeScope":"direct","authored":true}],"recurringEvents":[{"slug":"crown-audience","title":"The Queen’s Open Audience","dayOfWeek":2,"startMinute":600,"endMinute":780,"locationSlug":"ember-throne-hall","participants":["queen-maerra-vaelorian","prince-lucien-vaelorian","dame-ysabet-rooke","high-flame-elowen-orison"],"rhythm":"Petitions begin orderly and grow dangerous as testimony crosses caste lines.","hooks":["A petition names an absent character.","The throne reacts to an oath."]},{"slug":"velvet-masks","title":"The Veiled Supper","dayOfWeek":5,"startMinute":1260,"endMinute":1500,"locationSlug":"house-of-velvet-oaths","participants":["sabine-silk-veyl","lady-isolde-morcant","tamsin-quill"],"rhythm":"Masked guests exchange art, desire, and information under Compact law.","hooks":["A guest uses a forbidden royal seal.","A private contract reaches the wrong table."]},{"slug":"red-reeds-council","title":"The Red Reeds Workers’ Council","dayOfWeek":4,"startMinute":960,"endMinute":1080,"locationSlug":"house-red-reeds","participants":["maeve-redreed","brina-forgehand","sera-blackvein"],"rhythm":"Workers vote on safety, barred patrons, wages, and the coming mutiny before the night crowd arrives.","hooks":["A vote divides the house.","A worker requests passage south."]},{"slug":"crimson-banquet","title":"Crimson Veil Masked Banquet","dayOfWeek":5,"startMinute":1320,"endMinute":1560,"locationSlug":"crimson-veil","participants":["celessa-vane","queen-selene-ravaryn","prince-aurel-ravaryn","ilyra-ashscale"],"rhythm":"Formal performance and private bargaining blur while boundaries remain ritualized and visible.","hooks":["Two masks are exchanged.","A dragon cry interrupts a political toast."]},{"slug":"rootmarket-bell","title":"Rootmarket Commons Bell","dayOfWeek":6,"startMinute":480,"endMinute":720,"locationSlug":"rootmarket","participants":["duchess-aveline-edevane","thalia-moss","nerys-rowanleaf","lyssa-bramble"],"rhythm":"Trade pauses for public notices, missing names, song, and disputes judged by mixed-caste witnesses.","hooks":["Tax collectors arrive.","A living record changes during testimony."]},{"slug":"dead-tide-court","title":"Dead-Tide Court","dayOfWeek":3,"startMinute":1020,"endMinute":1200,"locationSlug":"drowned-crown-palace","participants":["duchess-mirelle-greymere","lord-cassian-greymere","admiral-nyra-greymere"],"rhythm":"Greymere hears disputes at the lowest tide, with proceedings ending when water crosses the green line.","hooks":["A case cannot finish before the tide.","A sealed sea door opens."]},{"slug":"lantern-change","title":"The Lantern Change","dayOfWeek":5,"startMinute":1080,"endMinute":1140,"locationSlug":"lantern-rooms","participants":["delphine-lantern","captain-seraphine-vale","orla-saye"],"rhythm":"Workers set evening boundaries and exchange route warnings before clients enter.","hooks":["A red lantern is hung for a royal name.","A route signal contradicts Orla’s weather reading."]},{"slug":"unshackled-debate","title":"The Unshackled Debate","dayOfWeek":4,"startMinute":1140,"endMinute":1320,"locationSlug":"unshackled-cup","participants":["asha-ren","nia-chainbreaker","joren-ash","malrec-vale"],"rhythm":"Any adult may speak once before anyone speaks twice; arguments influence faction mood but never force outcomes.","hooks":["A noble envoy invokes market peace.","A speaker questions Asha’s hidden authority."]},{"slug":"glass-echo-watch","title":"The Glass Echo Watch","dayOfWeek":0,"startMinute":1020,"endMinute":1170,"locationSlug":"glass-battlefield","participants":["petra-glass","rhevan-crownsbane","sister-mercy-voss"],"rhythm":"Guides and witnesses record the weekly sunset echo before wind destroys its newest fragments.","hooks":["A familiar voice appears.","The echo addresses a current listener."]},{"slug":"saintless-blue-flame","title":"The Blue-Flame Chosen-Name Rite","dayOfWeek":6,"startMinute":1200,"endMinute":1320,"locationSlug":"saintless-house","participants":["liora-saintless","nia-chainbreaker","asha-ren"],"rhythm":"Participants may burn an imposed title or name before witnesses; no disclosure is required.","hooks":["A royal title refuses to burn.","A signet opens when placed near the flame."]}],"storyArcs":[{"slug":"the-ashen-crown","title":"The Ashen Crown","premise":"Asha Renn’s imperial identity can unite the realm, invalidate every claimant, or turn the rebellion into another dynasty.","involved":["asha-ren","queen-maerra-vaelorian","prince-lucien-vaelorian","sister-mercy-voss","liora-saintless","rhevan-crownsbane"],"coreFacts":["Asha is Othmar’s surviving child.","Othmar’s memory names her successor only within an elective covenant.","Her signet opens the Vault.","Maerra tried to save her during the Feast."],"stages":["Find the living execution record.","Recover Othmar’s memory vial.","Decide whether Asha learns privately or publicly.","Reach the Vault with a willing witness."],"possibleEndStates":["Asha claims a constitutional crown.","Asha renounces the throne and helps unmake hereditary rule.","A rival exposes her before she can choose.","Her identity remains secret while the rebellion wins by other means."]},{"slug":"three-unhatched-fires","title":"Three Unhatched Fires","premise":"Sun, Cinder, and Verdant eggs will hatch only when the relevant forms of ownership are surrendered in their presence.","involved":["ilyra-ashscale","rhevan-crownsbane","thalia-moss","prince-aurel-ravaryn","queen-selene-ravaryn","orla-saye"],"coreFacts":["The Cinder egg hears captive dragons.","The Verdant egg responds to surrendered land claims.","The Sun egg requires a valid claimant to renounce inherited right.","Vaulkar intends to test, not crown, humanity."],"stages":["Locate all three eggs.","Learn each refusal condition.","Protect them from the crowns.","Choose separate hatchings or a single covenant rite."],"possibleEndStates":["A restored free dragon conclave.","One house seizes a hatchling.","The eggs remain sleeping by mutual choice.","Vaulkar destroys the hatchery and leaves humanity without dragon alliance."]},{"slug":"feast-of-falling-embers","title":"The Feast of Falling Embers","premise":"The massacre was not one conspiracy but three overlapping plots whose collisions killed the imperial family.","involved":["queen-maerra-vaelorian","queen-selene-ravaryn","prince-lucien-vaelorian","sabine-silk-veyl","celessa-vane","kael-dravos","admiral-nyra-greymere","malrec-vale"],"coreFacts":["Maerra received a warning.","Lucien burned evidence implicating their mother.","Kael carried poisoned wine unknowingly.","Nyra transported an assassin unknowingly.","Selene destroyed a renunciation declaration.","The imperial prince planned to end hereditary succession."],"stages":["Decode Sabine’s gown measurements.","Match ship, wine, and guest records.","Recover Celessa’s declaration.","Confront the surviving architects separately."],"possibleEndStates":["A public truth commission.","A claimant weaponizes only the portion harming rivals.","The truth is sealed to preserve a fragile peace.","Survivors confess and destroy every existing claim."]},{"slug":"deepnail-awakening","title":"The Dragon Beneath Deepnail","premise":"The mine’s star-metal is the living skeleton of an ancient dragon whose awakening can free the miners or collapse the March.","involved":["sera-blackvein","brina-forgehand","princess-elara-thornwall","lord-halric-thornwall","thalia-moss","nia-chainbreaker"],"coreFacts":["The ore carries a pulse and Name.","Dragon bolts use stolen covenant bone.","The western ventilation shaft can evacuate families.","The Chain Legions will revolt if their families are freed."],"stages":["Map the speaking chamber.","Secure ventilation and family routes.","Sabotage or seize the dragon-bolt works.","Choose whether to wake, heal, or mercifully end the buried dragon."],"possibleEndStates":["Deepnail becomes a free city.","The mine collapses after evacuation.","Halric binds the dragon into a weapon.","The dragon wakes and destroys Thornwall Keep."]},{"slug":"the-red-ledger","title":"The Red Ledger","premise":"Morcant’s hidden archive can prove that caste and noble bloodlines were systematically falsified.","involved":["lady-isolde-morcant","tamsin-quill","brina-forgehand","nerys-rowanleaf","malrec-vale","queen-maerra-vaelorian"],"coreFacts":["Highblood lines include erased Chainborn ancestors.","Tamsin’s guild mark is forged.","Brina’s family freedom rests on a forgery.","The Sevenfold registers were rewritten retroactively."],"stages":["Reach the dye-stall stair.","Compare living leaves with red ledgers.","Protect witnesses from every implicated house.","Choose release, selective leverage, or public burning."],"possibleEndStates":["The caste system loses genealogical legitimacy.","Isolde establishes a new information regime.","Riots destroy records needed by displaced families.","A claimant uses the evidence to purge rival houses."]},{"slug":"unbound-hymn","title":"The Unbound Hymn","premise":"The original hymn depicts Serath breaking chains rather than sanctifying obedience, and its Name-charged melody may transform law when sung publicly.","involved":["high-flame-elowen-orison","brother-aldren","lyssa-bramble","asha-ren","liora-saintless"],"coreFacts":["The eighth brazier reveals erased scripture.","Aldren’s trial notes preserve Asha’s family name.","Lyssa’s melody awakens collective Name magic.","Coerced listeners could become unwilling ritual participants."],"stages":["Light the eighth brazier.","Reconstruct text and melody.","Choose witnesses who can freely join.","Perform, publish, or suppress the hymn."],"possibleEndStates":["A voluntary realm-wide liberation rite.","A church schism with local reforms.","A coercive mass working that damages the cause.","Elowen reforms the hierarchy from within."]},{"slug":"the-prison-fleet","title":"The Prison Fleet","premise":"Ravaryn transports are preparing to move thousands of captives before peace negotiations can restrict the trade.","involved":["delphine-lantern","kael-dravos","admiral-nyra-greymere","captain-seraphine-vale","idris-salt","bastian-crow"],"coreFacts":["Tidevault sells prisoners to Ravaryn.","The Lantern route map was copied.","Kael plans to seize the transports.","Bastian’s hidden fleet is incomplete."],"stages":["Identify the route-map traitor.","Empty or hold Tidevault.","Choose stealth evacuation or open fleet revolt.","Reach a safe harbor before the storm closes."],"possibleEndStates":["A free refugee fleet.","A disastrous naval battle.","Nyra defects with the western crews.","Mirelle trades independence for safe passage."]},{"slug":"roots-outlive-crowns","title":"Roots Outlive Crowns","premise":"Aveline’s secret awakening order and Rowan’s neutral defense plan cannot both survive invasion.","involved":["duchess-aveline-edevane","lord-rowan-edevane","freya-hart","thalia-moss","princess-elara-thornwall","king-edric-thornwall"],"coreFacts":["Aveline authorized dragon waking under specific conditions.","Rowan’s forged evidence caused a courier death.","The forest corridor covers three sleeping dragons.","Both northern and southern armies need Reach grain."],"stages":["Recover the courier message.","Confront the siblings with shared evidence.","Redirect, starve, or negotiate with invading forces.","Decide whether waking the forest is defense or catastrophe."],"possibleEndStates":["A representative Reach compact.","Verdant dragons overgrow the stone roads.","Rowan secures armed neutrality.","Aveline becomes a revolutionary sovereign despite herself."]},{"slug":"what-sinks-shall-rise","title":"What Sinks Shall Rise","premise":"The Greymere autonomy charter can free the coast, enrich a claimant, or expose centuries of imperial fraud.","involved":["duchess-mirelle-greymere","lord-cassian-greymere","orla-saye","bastian-crow","queen-maerra-vaelorian","queen-selene-ravaryn"],"coreFacts":["The charter lies beneath the submerged throne room.","Cassian promised it to two crowns.","A dead tide opens the chamber.","Myrrix’s scale can protect one descent."],"stages":["Predict the dead tide.","Choose who enters the flooded palace.","Recover and authenticate the charter.","Decide whether recognition is asked, declared, or made irrelevant."],"possibleEndStates":["Independent abolitionist coast.","Greymere vassalage under Maerra or Selene.","Captain-rule without hereditary house authority.","The charter is lost and legitimacy built through present consent."]},{"slug":"the-glassing-command","title":"The Glassing Command","premise":"Battlefield echoes can establish who ordered the catastrophe and why the dragons rebelled.","involved":["petra-glass","rhevan-crownsbane","king-edric-thornwall","lady-rowena-thornwall","dame-ysabet-rooke","sister-mercy-voss"],"coreFacts":["Edric issued the command after refusal.","Petra’s mother answered from a dragon saddle.","Rowena’s requisitions prove the offensive was planned.","Rhevan carries the dying dragon’s memory."],"stages":["Map four echo positions.","Survive the ash-lightning center.","Compare living memory to logistical evidence.","Publish, bargain, or prosecute."],"possibleEndStates":["Edric stands public trial.","Halric suppresses the evidence and accelerates war.","Elara assumes a reformist northern crown.","The March rejects monarchy through soldiers’ councils."]},{"slug":"velvet-law","title":"The Velvet Law","premise":"Five pleasure houses can unite their worker protections into realm-wide law, but crown recognition threatens autonomy.","involved":["sabine-silk-veyl","maeve-redreed","celessa-vane","delphine-lantern","liora-saintless","lady-isolde-morcant"],"coreFacts":["The Compact already shares barred-client and safe-route records.","Each house protects a different caste and jurisdiction.","A royal patron’s violation can force a public case.","Morcant contracts can bind recognition if no crown loophole remains."],"stages":["Win ratification from all five houses.","Expose the violating patron with worker consent.","Draft law separating labor, shelter, and intimacy.","Choose crown statute, guild charter, or independent compact."],"possibleEndStates":["Realm-wide enforceable worker autonomy.","A licensed but surveilled system.","Independent houses become political sanctuaries.","The network fractures over secrecy and public testimony."]},{"slug":"the-scarlet-marriage","title":"The Scarlet Marriage","premise":"Halric and Selene’s secret marriage compact would merge the Chain Legions, western dragons, and two claims against Aurelis.","involved":["lord-halric-thornwall","queen-selene-ravaryn","princess-elara-thornwall","prince-aurel-ravaryn","queen-maerra-vaelorian","lady-isolde-morcant"],"coreFacts":["Halric offered to displace Aurel.","Selene has not accepted but is preparing terms.","The compact preserves dragon captivity and hereditary bondage.","Both parties privately expect to betray the other."],"stages":["Find the hidden drafts.","Learn Aurel and Elara’s responses.","Sabotage, expose, renegotiate, or permit the union.","Survive the military mobilization triggered by discovery."],"possibleEndStates":["The compact collapses both dynasties.","A terrifying dual monarchy.","Elara and Aurel publicly renounce their houses’ terms.","Maerra preempts the alliance with reform or war."]}],"worldFacts":[{"slug":"history-01","title":"The Age Without Thrones: Before 0 AF","factText":"Dragons and human river-cities share the continent through local compacts. No hereditary sovereign may command a dragon; riders are chosen for a season and judged by a conclave.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","the-age-without-thrones"],"triggerTerms":["The Age Without Thrones","Before 0 AF"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":30,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-02","title":"The First Covenant: 0 AF","factText":"A famine and sky-war end when the dragon Azhuriel bargains with seven human city-states. The covenant forbids ownership of persons, compels dragons to choose riders freely, and requires rulers to surrender power when rejected by the conclave.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","the-first-covenant"],"triggerTerms":["The First Covenant","0 AF"],"minWorldFamiliarity":2,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":30,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-03","title":"The First Empire: 19 AF","factText":"Ardan Vaelorian unites the city-states after being chosen by three dragons. His provisional war-crown becomes the Ember Throne, and temporary authority quietly hardens into dynasty.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","the-first-empire"],"triggerTerms":["The First Empire","19 AF"],"minWorldFamiliarity":4,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":30,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-04","title":"The Sevenfold Decree: 113 AF","factText":"Empress Calistra divides society into Seven Steps. Priests declare the hierarchy divine. The lowest step is described as temporary penance; within two generations it becomes hereditary bondage.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","the-sevenfold-decree"],"triggerTerms":["The Sevenfold Decree","113 AF"],"minWorldFamiliarity":6,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":30,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-05","title":"The Dragon Wars: 271 AF","factText":"Ravaryn breeders begin controlling eggs and separating hatchlings from wild elders. House Vaelorian wins the conflict but grants Ravaryn permanent custody of the imperial hatcheries.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","the-dragon-wars"],"triggerTerms":["The Dragon Wars","271 AF"],"minWorldFamiliarity":8,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":30,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-06","title":"The Chain Law: 412 AF","factText":"War debt, criminal punishment, and conquered status become inheritable. The Chainborn caste is transformed from limited penal service into chattel slavery enforced by crown, temple, and guild contract.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","the-chain-law"],"triggerTerms":["The Chain Law","412 AF"],"minWorldFamiliarity":10,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":30,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-07","title":"The Drowned Rebellion: 603 AF","factText":"House Greymere attempts to abolish hereditary bondage in its ports. The imperial fleet destroys Greymere’s navy and drowns part of its island seat with dragonfire-heated tides.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","the-drowned-rebellion"],"triggerTerms":["The Drowned Rebellion","603 AF"],"minWorldFamiliarity":12,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":30,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-08","title":"The Silent Clutch: 689 AF","factText":"The last verified dragon egg fails to hatch. Priests blame moral decay among commoners; dragonkeepers privately suspect the covenant itself has been broken beyond endurance.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","the-silent-clutch"],"triggerTerms":["The Silent Clutch","689 AF"],"minWorldFamiliarity":14,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":30,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-09","title":"The Feast of Falling Embers: 701 AF","factText":"Emperor Othmar, his consort, and most direct heirs are murdered during a wedding feast. Three claimants raise crowns before the bodies cool. The War of Three Crowns begins.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"local","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","the-feast-of-falling-embers"],"triggerTerms":["The Feast of Falling Embers","701 AF"],"minWorldFamiliarity":16,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":30,"interactive":true},{"slug":"history-10","title":"The Glassing of Aster Field: 709 AF","factText":"Sun and Cinder Dragons clash above the imperial heartland. Forty miles of soil become black glass, refugees become Ashen by decree, and dragons on both sides refuse further massed battle.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"local","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","the-glassing-of-aster-field"],"triggerTerms":["The Glassing of Aster Field","709 AF"],"minWorldFamiliarity":18,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":30,"interactive":true},{"slug":"history-11","title":"The First Broken Chain: 715 AF","factText":"Enslaved miners seize Deepnail’s western shaft and hold it for nine days. The revolt is crushed, but the Broken Chain becomes a decentralized rebellion operating across every kingdom.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"local","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","the-first-broken-chain"],"triggerTerms":["The First Broken Chain","715 AF"],"minWorldFamiliarity":20,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":30,"interactive":true},{"slug":"history-12","title":"The Present Year: 718 AF","factText":"Three living dragon eggs are discovered; the Ember Throne answers to an unknown servant; Verdant roots break old roads; and the crowns prepare a peace summit each intends to weaponize.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"local","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","the-present-year"],"triggerTerms":["The Present Year","718 AF"],"minWorldFamiliarity":22,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":30,"interactive":true},{"slug":"caste-1","title":"The Crowned","factText":"May claim sovereign authority and petition for a dragon bond. A Crowned person rejected by a bonded dragon is considered spiritually suspect, though the law avoids saying so. In practice: Fewer than twenty people hold this status; legitimacy matters more than actual competence.","category":"institution","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["caste","seven-steps","the-crowned"],"triggerTerms":["The Crowned","caste","station","rank"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"caste-2","title":"The Highblood","factText":"May own estates, field armies, sit in high court, and sponsor formal magic. Cannot legally marry below the Bannerborn without crown dispensation. In practice: Great houses buy dispensations, hide children, and weaponize genealogy.","category":"institution","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["caste","seven-steps","the-highblood"],"triggerTerms":["The Highblood","caste","station","rank"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"caste-3","title":"The Bannerborn","factText":"May bear noble steel, command troops, hold minor land, enter royal administration, and testify against peers. Status depends on continuing service to crown, temple, or house. In practice: Knights and officials enforce a system that can erase them with one accusation.","category":"institution","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["caste","seven-steps","the-bannerborn"],"triggerTerms":["The Bannerborn","caste","station","rank"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"caste-4","title":"The Guildmarked","factText":"May own businesses, receive formal education, practice medicine, and study licensed lesser Names. Cannot command a feudal levy or purchase rural estates. In practice: The merchant elite are rich enough to influence nobles and too low-born to be respected by them.","category":"institution","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["caste","seven-steps","the-guildmarked"],"triggerTerms":["The Guildmarked","caste","station","rank"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"caste-5","title":"The Hearthfolk","factText":"May rent property, marry freely within the lower Steps, join militias, and petition local courts. Cannot carry long steel, learn Names, or testify alone against a noble. In practice: They produce most food, labor, and soldiers while possessing little leverage.","category":"institution","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["caste","seven-steps","the-hearthfolk"],"triggerTerms":["The Hearthfolk","caste","station","rank"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"caste-6","title":"The Ashen","factText":"May accept wages and temporary lodging where local law permits. May not own land, join guilds, bear arms, or travel without papers. In practice: Refugees, conquered peoples, bastards, discharged prisoners, and disgraced families can all be cast down into this Step.","category":"institution","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["caste","seven-steps","the-ashen"],"triggerTerms":["The Ashen","caste","station","rank"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"caste-7","title":"The Chainborn","factText":"Recognized only as possessing minimal sanctuary rights under temple law. Treated as inheritable property; movement, marriage, literacy, and family unity require permission. In practice: The system is sustained by noble estates, mines, military camps, shipping houses, and temple bureaucracy. Escape networks challenge it everywhere.","category":"institution","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"mature","topicTags":["caste","seven-steps","the-chainborn"],"triggerTerms":["The Chainborn","caste","station","rank"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"house-vaelorian-public","title":"House Vaelorian","factText":"Queen Maerra descends from Emperor Othmar’s elder sister and holds the imperial capital, archives, and Ember Throne. Its public aim is to restore one empire under codified law.","category":"politics","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["house","house-vaelorian","succession"],"triggerTerms":["House Vaelorian","Dragonbone Citadel","From Flame, Order."],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"house-thornwall-public","title":"House Thornwall","factText":"King Edric says Emperor Othmar named him Protector and successor during the first attack at the wedding feast. Its public aim is to replace decadent southern rule with disciplined northern kingship.","category":"politics","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["house","house-thornwall","succession"],"triggerTerms":["House Thornwall","Thornwall Keep","We Do Not Bend."],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"house-ravaryn-public","title":"House Ravaryn","factText":"Queen Selene is widow to Othmar’s eldest son and rules for Prince Aurel, the senior surviving male-line descendant. Its public aim is to crown aurel and restore the dragon empire from the west.","category":"politics","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["house","house-ravaryn","succession"],"triggerTerms":["House Ravaryn","Pyrehold Castle","The Sky Belongs to Us."],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"house-morcant-public","title":"House Morcant","factText":"No crown claim; the house claims the right to certify debts, bloodlines, and treaty seals. Its public aim is to preserve commerce and prevent any claimant from destroying the tax base.","category":"politics","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["house","house-morcant","succession"],"triggerTerms":["House Morcant","The Red Ledger Exchange","Every Truth Has Its Price."],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"house-greymere-public","title":"House Greymere","factText":"Greymere claims sovereign independence over the coast rather than the imperial throne. Its public aim is to rebuild the coast and gain formal independence.","category":"politics","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["house","house-greymere","succession"],"triggerTerms":["House Greymere","Drowned Crown Palace","What Sinks Shall Rise."],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"house-edevane-public","title":"House Edevane","factText":"No public crown claim; the family presents itself as neutral steward of the realm’s breadbasket. Its public aim is to keep roads open and civilians fed regardless of banner.","category":"politics","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["house","house-edevane","succession"],"triggerTerms":["House Edevane","Hartwood Hall","Roots Outlive Crowns."],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1.2,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":true},{"slug":"house-vaelorian-secret","title":"The hidden fault of House Vaelorian","factText":"The Vaelorian archive holds an uncensored copy of the First Covenant proving hereditary monarchy violates dragon law.","category":"scandal","truthMode":"secret","knowledgeScope":"story","contentLevel":"mature","topicTags":["house-secret","house-vaelorian"],"triggerTerms":["House Vaelorian","Dragonbone Citadel"],"minWorldFamiliarity":35,"requiredStorySlug":"the-ashen-crown","weight":1.4,"cooldownTurns":60,"interactive":true},{"slug":"house-thornwall-secret","title":"The hidden fault of House Thornwall","factText":"Edric’s succession testament was produced after the emperor died and bears ink made six months later.","category":"scandal","truthMode":"secret","knowledgeScope":"story","contentLevel":"mature","topicTags":["house-secret","house-thornwall"],"triggerTerms":["House Thornwall","Thornwall Keep"],"minWorldFamiliarity":35,"requiredStorySlug":"roots-outlive-crowns","weight":1.4,"cooldownTurns":60,"interactive":true},{"slug":"house-ravaryn-secret","title":"The hidden fault of House Ravaryn","factText":"The hatchery poisoned wild nesting grounds to preserve its monopoly and helped cause the Silent Clutch.","category":"scandal","truthMode":"secret","knowledgeScope":"story","contentLevel":"mature","topicTags":["house-secret","house-ravaryn"],"triggerTerms":["House Ravaryn","Pyrehold Castle"],"minWorldFamiliarity":35,"requiredStorySlug":"three-unhatched-fires","weight":1.4,"cooldownTurns":60,"interactive":true},{"slug":"house-morcant-secret","title":"The hidden fault of House Morcant","factText":"Morcant records can prove that several celebrated Highblood lines descend from people later declared Chainborn.","category":"scandal","truthMode":"secret","knowledgeScope":"story","contentLevel":"mature","topicTags":["house-secret","house-morcant"],"triggerTerms":["House Morcant","The Red Ledger Exchange"],"minWorldFamiliarity":35,"requiredStorySlug":"the-red-ledger","weight":1.4,"cooldownTurns":60,"interactive":true},{"slug":"house-greymere-secret","title":"The hidden fault of House Greymere","factText":"The flooded foundations contain the imperial charter proving Greymere was promised autonomy centuries ago.","category":"scandal","truthMode":"secret","knowledgeScope":"story","contentLevel":"mature","topicTags":["house-secret","house-greymere"],"triggerTerms":["House Greymere","Drowned Crown Palace"],"minWorldFamiliarity":35,"requiredStorySlug":"what-sinks-shall-rise","weight":1.4,"cooldownTurns":60,"interactive":true},{"slug":"house-edevane-secret","title":"The hidden fault of House Edevane","factText":"Edevane root-priests can wake the Verdant Dragons, but doing so may destroy every stone city in their path.","category":"scandal","truthMode":"secret","knowledgeScope":"story","contentLevel":"mature","topicTags":["house-secret","house-edevane"],"triggerTerms":["House Edevane","Hartwood Hall"],"minWorldFamiliarity":35,"requiredStorySlug":"roots-outlive-crowns","weight":1.4,"cooldownTurns":60,"interactive":true},{"slug":"place-secret-dragonbone-citadel","title":"Hidden truth: Dragonbone Citadel","factText":"The deepest rib chamber preserves Azhuriel’s final memory of the uncrowned covenant.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"secret","knowledgeScope":"story","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"crownspire","locationSlug":"dragonbone-citadel","topicTags":["location-secret","dragonbone-citadel","crownspire"],"triggerTerms":["Dragonbone Citadel","royal audiences","court intrigue"],"minWorldFamiliarity":25,"weight":1.1,"cooldownTurns":45,"interactive":true},{"slug":"place-secret-ember-throne-hall","title":"Hidden truth: The Hall of the Ember Throne","factText":"The throne recently ignited for a Chainborn attendant named only Lark.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"secret","knowledgeScope":"story","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"crownspire","locationSlug":"ember-throne-hall","topicTags":["location-secret","ember-throne-hall","crownspire"],"triggerTerms":["The Hall of the Ember Throne","petitions","trials"],"minWorldFamiliarity":25,"weight":1.1,"cooldownTurns":45,"interactive":true},{"slug":"place-secret-gilded-steps-market","title":"Hidden truth: Gilded Steps Market","factText":"A sealed stair beneath the dye stalls reaches Morcant’s hidden archive.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"secret","knowledgeScope":"story","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"crownspire","locationSlug":"gilded-steps-market","topicTags":["location-secret","gilded-steps-market","crownspire"],"triggerTerms":["Gilded Steps Market","shopping","street food"],"minWorldFamiliarity":25,"weight":1.1,"cooldownTurns":45,"interactive":true},{"slug":"place-secret-house-of-velvet-oaths","title":"Hidden truth: House of Velvet Oaths","factText":"The house holds a ciphered copy of the guest list from the Feast of Falling Embers.","category":"adult","truthMode":"secret","knowledgeScope":"story","contentLevel":"mature","districtSlug":"crownspire","locationSlug":"house-of-velvet-oaths","topicTags":["location-secret","house-of-velvet-oaths","crownspire"],"triggerTerms":["House of Velvet Oaths","drinks","music"],"minWorldFamiliarity":25,"weight":1.1,"cooldownTurns":45,"interactive":true},{"slug":"place-secret-basilica-seven-flames","title":"Hidden truth: Basilica of Seven Flames","factText":"Lighting the eighth brazier reveals erased lines in every sacred inscription nearby.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"secret","knowledgeScope":"story","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"crownspire","locationSlug":"basilica-seven-flames","topicTags":["location-secret","basilica-seven-flames","crownspire"],"triggerTerms":["Basilica of Seven Flames","worship","confession"],"minWorldFamiliarity":25,"weight":1.1,"cooldownTurns":45,"interactive":true},{"slug":"place-